SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR WTFPL

One carve out, and it is not optional. The Markov model, the transliteration rule
tables and the test fixtures in this repository are not mine to relicense. They come
from Google's myanmar-tools and remain under the Apache License 2.0, which requires
that its attribution travel with them. See NOTICE and
src/vendor/LICENSE-myanmar-tools.md. Picking WTFPL for the rest does not change that.

Specifically, these stay Apache-2.0:

  src/vendor/markov.ts
  src/vendor/translit.ts
  src/vendor/model-data.ts
  src/vendor/zawgyiUnicodeModel.dat
  src/vendor/translit/*
  shared/*
  python/src/jawgyi/markov.py
  python/src/jawgyi/convert.py
  python/src/jawgyi/data/*
  test/fixtures/*

Everything else is yours under either license below.

